# org-target: docs/10-19-design/10-architecture/10.24-sysml-interoperability-and-authority-boundaries.org::#sysml-interoperability
# render-layout: elk; theme: 0; pad: 24; timeout: 30
direction: down
library: "Native Scheme Library\nCatalog / POO Module / Profile / Scenario\nOwns extensible models and obligations"
projection: "Optional SysML v2 projection\nNamed mapping and explicit unmapped constructs\nExact profile, model and imported-library bytes"
tool: "Isolated OpenSysML method\nParse / instantiate / explicit assertion\nRaw verdict, engine, bounds and executable identity"
oracle: "Independent control\nTruth table / mapping oracle / negative cases\nQNT correspondence for behavior; Rust checks for implementation"
ascent: "Existing ASCENT Evidence DSL\nRegister scoped external observations\nKeep counters, pending and method applicability"
aitia: "Existing Aitia and Core\nFresh current verification required\nImported satisfaction is never approval or receipt authority"
views: "English Org + D2\nHuman architectural view\nTool benefit, maintenance cost and open gates"
library -> projection -> tool -> ascent -> aitia
library -> oracle -> ascent
projection -> views
tool -> views
